-- Nine Iron Juggernauts of Tolkeen and seven cyborg bodies, as vessel rows.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
-- Rifts Book of Magic, printed 343-347: the Blazing, Earthwake, Fury,
-- Iron-Dragonfly, Sea Viper, Thundering, Warhawk, Wing Blade and Millipede
-- Iron Juggernauts. The book's first full inventory (2026-10-03, in its
-- survey) found the catalog held none of them. They are `robot`, as the seven
-- Federation of Magic automatons the same chapter prints are.
-- Rifts World Book 8: Japan, printed 101-109: the four Dragon 'Borg bodies.
-- Rifts World Book 25: China 2, printed 128-132: the three Geo-Borg bodies.
-- The seven classes for those bodies exist and carry M.D.C. by location and
-- built-in weapons as prose; these are the bodies as `borg` rows, the shape
-- Warlords of Russia gave its cyborgs (PR #1617) the day after Japan shipped.
-- The classes are NOT rewired here: each still describes its body in prose.
--
-- EVERY NUMBER WAS READ OFF A RENDER and checked against a render again by
-- book-reconcile: about 700 figures, none wrong. Every slug was queried
-- against production vehicles, gear and imported_classes first.
--
-- CONVENTIONS (as the Triax 2 and Warlords of Russia vessels):
--   cost is the lowest printed price, with the wording in cost_note; the
--     juggernauts print no price and are NULL.
--   Seven juggernauts print a Main Body figure and no location list, size or
--     weight; only the Wing Blade and the Millipede print locations.
--   A body's slug leads with its model number, so it cannot be mistaken for
--     its class id.
--   A dragon 'borg's tail prints a rate (50 M.D.C. per 6 ft), not a total: mdc
--     is NULL and the rate is in mdc_note.
--   Numbered items that are not weapons (training, feature lists, handheld
--     catalog weapons) are left out, so a 'borg's ordinals have gaps.
--   A book slip is stored as printed and named in the row: "P.P. 23" in two
--     hand to hand blocks whose bodies print P.P. 22, the Wing Blade tail's
--     (1.2 m), and the Millipede's page reference.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicles (slug, name, system, vehicle_class, crew, passengers, speed_ground, speed_air, speed_water, dimensions, weight_tons, mdc_main_body, is_mega_damage, ar, cost, cost_note, description, source_book) VALUES
('iron-juggernaut-blazing', 'Blazing Iron Juggernaut', 'rifts', 'robot', 'Uncertain. Intelligence suggests one human or D-Bee and one or two Elementals or primordial elemental force.', NULL, 'Running: 50 mph (80 km); double on a ley line. Leaping: 20 feet (6.1 m) high and 40 feet (12 m) long. Maximum range: unlimited.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 910, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Presumably millions of credits, but it acts and thinks like a living being, so it is less a possession or machine and more of a supernatural being made of iron and elemental fury. Not available for sale, although the Splugorth would love to get a few for their gladiatorial arenas.', 'A fire-wreathed Tolkeen war machine classed as an Iron Juggernaut TW Combat Robot, first described in Coalition Wars One p.81. It has supernatural P.S. 29, P.P. 22 and an I.Q. of 7-14, takes six physical attacks or two spells a melee round, and is +3 on initiative, +6 to strike with punches and kicks, +4 to strike at range, +3 to parry and dodge, +4 to pull punch, +1 to roll, +10 vs Horror Factor and +6 vs mind control. It speaks only in crackling 3-6 word phrases, sees clearly for a mile (1.6 km) with 180 degree peripheral vision and 2,000 foot (610 m) nightvision, sees the invisible, understands every language and never tires, eats or breathes.', 'Rifts Book of Magic p.343-344'),
('iron-juggernaut-earthwake', 'Earthwake Iron Juggernaut', 'rifts', 'robot', 'Uncertain. Intelligence suggests one human or D-Bee and one or two Elementals or primordial elemental force.', NULL, 'Running: 60 mph (96 km); double on a ley line. Leaping: 15 feet (4.6 m) high and 30 feet (9.1 m) long; double that from a running start, and double it again on a ley line. Maximum range: unlimited.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1187, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Presumably millions of credits, but it acts and thinks like a living being, so it is less a possession or machine and more of a supernatural being made of iron and elemental fury. Not available for sale, although the Splugorth would love to get a few for their gladiatorial arenas.', 'An amphibious earth-and-water Iron Juggernaut of Tolkeen, classed as a TW Combat Robot and first described in Coalition Wars Three p.74. It has supernatural P.S. 42, P.P. 22 and an I.Q. of 6-14 and takes nine physical attacks (seven in the water) or two spells a melee round; underwater it is +1 on initiative, +5 to strike, +3 to parry, +2 to automatic dodge, +4 to pull punch and +2 to roll, all doubled on dry land where the automatic dodge becomes an ordinary +4 dodge, with +10 vs Horror Factor and +8 vs mind control. It sees two miles (3.2 km) and through dark, murky water, has 180 degree peripheral vision and 3,000 foot (914 m) nightvision, sees the invisible, understands all languages, navigates on land at 98%, senses depth and water temperature and finds water within 50 miles (80 km) at 88%.', 'Rifts Book of Magic p.344'),
('iron-juggernaut-fury', 'Fury Iron Juggernaut', 'rifts', 'robot', 'Uncertain. Intelligence suggests one human or D-Bee and one or two Elementals or primordial elemental force.', NULL, 'Running: 50 mph (80 km); double on a ley line. It is a tracked all-terrain vehicle and can climb inclines as steep as 90 degrees. Maximum range: unlimited.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1340, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Presumably millions of credits, but it acts and thinks like a living being, so it is less a possession or machine and more of a supernatural being made of iron and elemental fury. Not available for sale, although the Splugorth would love to get a few for their gladiatorial arenas. Printed under the heading Black Market Cost.', 'A tracked earth-and-air Iron Juggernaut of Tolkeen, classed as a TW Combat Robot and first described in Coalition Wars One p.86. It has supernatural P.S. 40, P.P. 24 and an I.Q. of 8-14, takes six physical attacks or two spells a melee round, and is +4 on initiative, +7 to strike with punches and kicks, +9 with its forearm blades, +3 with its ion cannons, +9 to parry, +2 to dodge, +8 to pull punch, +10 vs Horror Factor and +8 vs mind control. It rumbles out 3-6 word phrases, sees two miles (3.2 km) with 180 degree peripheral vision and 6,000 foot (1,829 m) nightvision, sees the invisible, understands all languages and needs no air, food, drink or rest.', 'Rifts Book of Magic p.344'),
('iron-juggernaut-iron-dragonfly', 'Iron-Dragonfly Heavy Air Juggernaut', 'rifts', 'robot', 'Uncertain. Intelligence suggests one human or D-Bee and one or two Elementals or primordial elemental force.', NULL, 'Running: 30 mph (48 km), double on a ley line. Leaping: 10 feet (3 m) high and 15 feet (4.6 m) long. Maximum range: unlimited.', 'Flying: 600 mph (960 km); double on a ley line. Max. altitude is 20,000 feet (6,096 m).', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1210, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Presumably millions of credits, but it acts and thinks like a living being, so it is less a possession or machine and more of a supernatural being made of iron and elemental fury. Not available for sale, although the Splugorth would love to get a few for their gladiatorial arenas.', 'Tolkeen''s heavy flying Iron Juggernaut, classed as a TW Combat Robot and first described in Coalition Wars Three p.68; it outflies SAMAS, most flying power armor and many aircraft. It has supernatural P.S. 35, P.P. 20 and an I.Q. of 7-14, takes six physical attacks or two spells a melee round, and is +2 on initiative, +7 to strike with punches and kicks (+3 with energy blasts), +10 to parry, +3 to dodge (+5 in flight), +5 to pull punch, +1 to roll, +9 vs Horror Factor and +6 vs mind control. Its voice is a roaring wind limited to 1-6 word phrases; it sees three miles (4.8 km) and through smoke, has 180 degree peripheral vision and 6,000 foot (1,829 m) nightvision, sees the invisible and understands all languages.', 'Rifts Book of Magic p.345'),
('iron-juggernaut-sea-viper', 'Sea Viper Iron Juggernaut', 'rifts', 'robot', 'Uncertain. Intelligence suggests one human or D-Bee and one or two Elementals or primordial elemental force.', NULL, 'Running: 35 mph (56 km). On dry land a leap is 10 feet (3 m) high or 20 feet (6.1 m) lengthwise. Maximum range: unlimited.', NULL, 'Underwater: 100 mph (160 km or 86 knots); double that on a ley line. Can dive at double speed for up to 1,000 feet (305 m). Maximum depth tolerance is three miles (4.8 km). Can remain underwater indefinitely. Leaping: 20 feet (6.1 m) high and 60 feet (18.3 m) long; double if swimming at top speed and double again when swimming along a ley line.', NULL, NULL, 690, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Presumably millions of credits, but it acts and thinks like a living being, so it is less a possession or machine and more of a supernatural being made of iron and elemental fury. Not available for sale, although the Splugorth would love to get a few for their gladiatorial arenas.', 'Tolkeen''s underwater Iron Juggernaut, classed as a TW Combat Robot and first described in Coalition Wars Three p.70. It has supernatural P.S. 24, P.P. 22 and an I.Q. of 7-14 and takes eight physical attacks (six out of the water) or two spells a melee round; in the water it is +4 on initiative, +10 to strike, +8 to parry, +6 to automatic dodge, +6 to pull punch, +4 to disarm, +2 to roll, +10 vs Horror Factor and +6 vs mind control, and every bonus is halved on land. It speaks in deep phrases of up to eight words, sees two miles (3.2 km) and through smoke with 280 degree peripheral vision and 6,000 foot (1,829 m) nightvision, sees the invisible, understands all languages, senses water depth and magnetic north, navigates underwater at 98% and has sonic echo-location.', 'Rifts Book of Magic p.345'),
('iron-juggernaut-thundering', 'Thundering Iron Juggernaut', 'rifts', 'robot', 'Uncertain. Intelligence suggests one human or D-Bee and one or two Elementals or primordial elemental force.', NULL, 'Running: 100 mph (160 km); double on a ley line. Leaping: 60 feet (18.3 m) high and 120 feet (36.6 m) long; double when on a ley line. Maximum range: unlimited.', 'Flying: 60 mph (96 km) only on a ley line. Triple speed when riding during a Ley Line Storm.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1130, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Presumably millions of credits, but it acts and thinks like a living being, so it is less a possession or machine and more of a supernatural being made of iron and elemental fury. Not available for sale, although the Splugorth would love to get a few for their gladiatorial arenas.', 'A fast storm-and-air Iron Juggernaut of Tolkeen, classed as a TW Combat Robot and first described in Coalition Wars One p.83. It has supernatural P.S. 34, P.P. 26 and an I.Q. of 7-14, takes nine physical attacks or three spells a melee round, and is +6 on initiative, +9 to strike with punches and kicks, +11 with its forearm blades, +3 with energy weapons, +7 to parry, +5 to dodge, +6 to pull punch, +2 to roll, +10 vs Horror Factor and +6 vs mind control. It sees two miles (3.2 km) and through smoke, has 180 degree peripheral vision and 6,000 foot (1,829 m) nightvision, sees the invisible, understands all languages and never breathes, eats, drinks or tires.', 'Rifts Book of Magic p.345-346'),
('iron-juggernaut-warhawk', 'Warhawk Iron Juggernaut', 'rifts', 'robot', 'Uncertain. Intelligence suggests one human or D-Bee and one or two Elementals or primordial elemental force.', NULL, 'Running: 40 mph (64 km); double on a ley line. Leaping: 20 feet (6 m) high and 40 feet (12 m) across. Maximum range: unlimited.', 'Flying: 350 mph (560 km); double on a ley line. Max altitude is 15,000 feet (4,572 m).', NULL, NULL, NULL, 770, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Presumably millions of credits, but it acts and thinks like a living being, so it is less a possession or machine and more of a supernatural being made of iron and elemental fury. Not available for sale, although the Splugorth would love to get a few for their gladiatorial arenas.', 'A silent-flying fire-and-air Iron Juggernaut of Tolkeen, classed as a TW Combat Robot and first described in Coalition Wars Two p.61; it outperforms SAMAS, most power armor and some aircraft and prowls at 65%. It has supernatural P.S. 27, P.P. 23 and an I.Q. of 7-14, takes eight physical attacks or two spells a melee round, and is +3 on initiative, +9 to strike with punches and kicks, +4 with energy blasts, +7 to parry, +5 to dodge, +7 to automatic dodge while airborne, +6 to pull punch, +3 to roll, +9 vs Horror Factor and +6 vs mind control. It whispers hoarsely in phrases of under eight words, sees three miles (4.8 km) with 180 degree peripheral vision and 2,000 foot (610 m) nightvision, sees the invisible and understands all languages.', 'Rifts Book of Magic p.346'),
('iron-juggernaut-wing-blade', 'Wing Blade Iron Juggernaut', 'rifts', 'robot', 'Uncertain. Intelligence suggests one human or D-Bee and one or two Elementals or primordial elemental force.', NULL, 'Crawling: 30 mph (48 km; double on a ley line). Maximum range: unlimited.', 'Flying: 300 mph (480 km; double along ley lines). Altitude is 32,000 feet.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1480, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Presumably millions of credits, but it acts and thinks like a living being, so it is less a possession or machine and more of a supernatural being. No sale or availability line is printed.', 'A winged, many-legged ice-and-water Iron Juggernaut of Tolkeen that fights entirely with its blades, classed as a TW Combat Robot and first described in Coalition Wars 6: Final Siege p.59. It has supernatural P.S. 40, P.P. 26 and an I.Q. of 7-14, takes ten physical attacks or two spells a melee round, and is +6 on initiative, +10 to strike, +7 to parry, +5 to dodge, +6 to pull punch, +2 to roll, +10 vs Horror Factor and +6 vs mind control. It hisses 3-6 word phrases like escaping steam, has hawk-like sight to two miles (3.2 km), 180 degree peripheral vision and 6,000 foot (1829 m) nightvision, sees the invisible and understands all languages.', 'Rifts Book of Magic p.346-347'),
('iron-juggernaut-millipede', 'Millipede Iron Juggernaut', 'rifts', 'robot', 'Uncertain. Intelligence suggests one human or D-Bee and one or two Elementals or primordial elemental force.', NULL, 'Running: 100 mph (160 km; double on a ley line). Leaping: Not possible. Maximum range: unlimited.', 'Flying: Not possible.', 'Full underwater capabilities; no speed is printed.', '34 feet (10.4 m) tall, 32 feet (9.75 m) wide, and 90 feet (27.4 m) long.', NULL, 1880, 1, NULL, NULL, 'Presumably millions of credits, but it acts and thinks like a living being, so it is less a possession or machine and more of a supernatural being. No sale or availability line is printed.', 'The largest Iron Juggernaut in this book, a 90 foot, 38-legged earth machine that was massive and rare even in Tolkeen, classed as a TW Combat Robot and credited to Coalition Wars 6: Final Siege (the page reference is printed as p. 629). It has supernatural P.S. 40, P.P. 26 and an I.Q. of 7-14, takes twelve attacks a melee round, and is +5 on initiative, +9 to strike with punches, +5 with energy weapons, +4 to parry, +1 to dodge, +4 to pull punch, +10 vs Horror Factor and +5 vs mind control. It hisses 3-6 word phrases like steam, has hawk-like sight to two miles (3.2 km), 180 degree peripheral vision and 6,000 foot (1829 m) nightvision, sees the invisible and understands all languages.', 'Rifts Book of Magic p.347'),
('at-c8000-wing-blade-cyborg', 'AT-C8000 Wing Blade Dragon ''Borg', 'rifts', 'borg', 'One human volunteer.', NULL, 'Running: 120 mph (192 km). Leaping: 25 feet (7.6 m) high or lengthwise; a running leap adds 1D4x10 additional yards/meters.', 'Flying: Via jet pack only. The wings give +10% to the jet pack piloting skill; with one or both wings destroyed the ''borg can still fly on the detachable jet pack at -20% on piloting skill. No flying speed is printed.', NULL, 'Height: the bulk of the body stands five feet (1.5 m) tall; with wings folded and neck and head hung low, 7 feet (2.1 m) (5 feet/1.5 m when crouched); wings extended add 12 feet (3.6 m). Width: 2 1/2 feet (0.75 m) for the body itself, 3 1/2 feet (1 m) with the wings folded. Length: the neck adds six feet (1.8 m) and the tail another 12 feet (3.6 m), for a total length of 23 feet.', '1000 lbs (450 kg)', 270, 1, NULL, 6000000, 'Six million credits with all standard features and weapons. Poor availability; outside of the Republic only Ichto makes them, and at 10% more money. Armatech makes the dragon ''borgs exclusively for the military and police of the Republic of Japan; they are not available to the public.', 'The Republic of Japan''s espionage and light assault dragon body, nicknamed the Snoop: a slender, four-armed full conversion frame with folding bat wings, a long snaking neck for peering around corners and a bladed prehensile tail. It is equal to P.S. 24, P.P. 22 and Spd 176, runs on a nuclear supply with an average life of 20 years, and carries six video cameras in its neck and knees. This row is the body alone; the pilot is the class dragon-borg-wing-blade, which also lists the standard bionic features.', 'Rifts World Book 8: Japan p.101-102'),
('at-c9000-tsunami-cyborg', 'AT-C9000 Tsunami Dragon ''Borg', 'rifts', 'borg', 'One human volunteer.', NULL, 'Running: 120 mph (192 km). Leaping: 25 feet (7.6 m) high or lengthwise; a running leap adds 1D4x10 additional yards/meters.', 'Flying: Via jet pack only. 100 mph (160 kph) maximum speed. Range is limited to twelve hours at maximum speed before the jet pack needs to cool down; indefinite with rest stops and low speed (80 mph/108 kph or less, as printed). The wings give +10% to the jet pack piloting skill; with one or both wings destroyed the ''borg can still fly at -20% on piloting skill.', NULL, 'Height: 10 feet (3 m) when standing up straight (head to toes); the usual stooped posture reduces this to 7-8 feet (2.1 to 2.4 m). Width: 2 1/2 feet (0.75 m) for the body itself, 3 1/2 feet (1 m) with the wings folded. Length: the tail adds 6 feet (1.8 m), for a total length of 16 feet.', '1200 lbs (540 kg)', 320, 1, NULL, 8000000, 'Eight million credits with all standard features and weapons. Poor availability; outside of the Republic only Ichto makes them, and at 10% more money. Armatech makes the dragon ''borgs exclusively for the military and police of the Republic of Japan; they are not available to the public.', 'The second largest of the Republic of Japan''s dragon bodies, a heavy assault full conversion frame for army and police work with folding wings, a striking tail and a built-in jet pack. Its right arm ends in a mini-gun and vibro-axe instead of a hand, it is equal to P.S. 26, P.P. 23 and Spd 176, and its nuclear supply averages a 20 year life. This row is the body alone; the pilot is the class dragon-borg-tsunami, which also lists the standard bionic features and the insanity rolls. Printed 103 is a full-page illustration.', 'Rifts World Book 8: Japan p.102-105'),
('at-c10000-imperial-dragon-cyborg', 'AT-C10000 Imperial Dragon Combat ''Borg', 'rifts', 'borg', 'One human volunteer.', NULL, 'Running: 120 mph (192 km) on four legs; drops to 20 mph (32 kph) on two legs. Leaping: the snake body springs 30 feet (9 m) high or lengthwise; a running leap adds 1D4x10 additional yards/meters.', 'Flying: Not possible.', NULL, 'Height: 5 feet (1.5 m) while on all fours; rearing up on its hind legs it can stand 9 feet (2.7 m) tall. Width: 2 1/2 feet (0.75 m) for the body itself. Length: 24 feet (7.2 m) from head to tail.', '1500 lbs (675 kg)', 350, 1, NULL, 10000000, 'Ten million credits with all standard features and weapons. Poor availability; outside of the Republic only Ichto makes them, and at 10% more money. Armatech makes the dragon ''borgs exclusively for the military and police of the Republic of Japan; they are not available to the public.', 'A four-legged, serpentine heavy assault body that is a true dragon in shape rather than a humanoid, armed almost like a tank and fielded mostly by the Army of the New Republic. Its low profile and twisting frame suit guerrilla fighting on slopes no biped can climb; it is equal to P.S. 30, P.P. 22 and Spd 176 on a nuclear supply averaging 20 years. This row is the body alone; the pilot is the class dragon-borg-imperial-combat, which also lists the standard bionic features and the insanity rolls.', 'Rifts World Book 8: Japan p.105-107'),
('at-c12000-flame-cloud-cyborg', 'AT-C12000 Flame Cloud Dragon Attack ''Borg', 'rifts', 'borg', 'One human volunteer.', NULL, 'Running: 120 mph (192 km) on four legs; drops to 20 mph (32 kph) on two legs. Leaping: the snake body springs 30 feet (9 m) high or lengthwise; a running leap adds 1D4x10 additional yards/meters.', 'Flying: 500 mph (800 kph) maximum. At maximum speed (300-500 mph/480-800 kph) it cannot maneuver and flies in a straight line only: hitting it requires a called shot at -2, but it cannot parry or dodge. Cruising speed is 200 mph (320 kph). Range: maximum speeds for 8 hours before needing to cool off, or 24 hours at cruising speeds; indefinitely at cruising speeds with frequent rest stops. Destroying one jet thruster reduces maximum speed by 70% and the pilot is -25% to all rolls; destroying both grounds it, and if in the air it crashes.', NULL, 'Height: 5 feet (1.5 m) while on all fours; rearing up on its hind legs it can stand 9 feet (2.7 m) tall. Width: 2 1/2 feet (0.75 m) for the body itself; the jet thrusters add an additional 5 feet (1.5 m) to the sides. Length: 24 feet (7.2 m) from head to tail.', '1500 lbs (675 kg)', 320, 1, NULL, 12000000, 'Twelve million credits with all standard features and weapons. Poor availability; outside of the Republic only Ichto makes them, and at 10% more money. Armatech makes the dragon ''borgs exclusively for the military and police of the Republic of Japan; they are not available to the public.', 'The wingless flying version of the Imperial, a serpentine heavy air assault body carried by two side-mounted jet thrusters to near-supersonic speed and named for its diving plasma-breath strafing run. It is quick but clumsy until it slows to 60-100 mph (96-160 kph), is equal to P.S. 24, P.P. 22 and Spd 176, and runs on a nuclear supply averaging 20 years. This row is the body alone; the pilot is the class dragon-borg-flame-cloud, which also lists the standard bionic features and the insanity rolls.', 'Rifts World Book 8: Japan p.107-109'),
('db-800-demon-eater-cyborg', 'Demon-Eater Cyborg (DB-800)', 'rifts', 'borg', NULL, NULL, 'Running: 60 (96 km) in heavy armor, printed without a unit; in light or no armor speed is 100 mph (160 km). Leaping: up to 50 feet (15.2 m) up or across, double the distance with a running start at full speed. Wall-crawling: clings to and moves along walls and ceilings at half its maximum running speed.', 'Flying: Via jet pack only.', NULL, 'Height: 12 feet (3.7 m). Width at Shoulders: 4 feet (1.2 m).', 'One ton', 220, 1, NULL, 12000000, '12 million credits.', 'The Geofront''s heavy full conversion body, a twelve foot, twin-tailed machine styled as a demon so that it can stalk, ambush and fight real ones tooth and claw. It has Bionic P.S. 35, P.P. 24 and Speed 98, runs on nuclear power, and climbs sheer walls and ceilings on electro-magnets and climbing fibers, prowling there at 70% below Speed 22 (15 mph/24 km) and gaining +2 on initiative and +2 to strike when it drops on a foe by surprise; the heavy armor slows it and costs -50% to Prowl on the ground. This row is the body alone; the pilot is the class geofront-demon-eater-geo-borg, which also lists the standard bionic features.', 'Rifts World Book 25: China 2 p.128-130'),
('ab-830-assault-geo-borg', 'Assault Geo-Borg (AB-830)', 'rifts', 'borg', NULL, NULL, 'Running: 120 (192 km) in light armor, printed without a unit; without armor it can run at 140 mph (224 km). Heavy armor reduces speed by half (70 mph/112 km). Leaping: with the micro-boosters, up to 60 feet (18.3 m) high and 100 feet (30.5 m) across (half that distance without the boosters).', 'Flying: Via jet pack only.', NULL, 'Height: 7 feet (2.1 m). Width: 2.5 feet (.7 m).', '600 lbs (270 kg)', 180, 1, NULL, 8000000, '8 million credits.', 'The Geofront''s stealth and infiltration full conversion body, built to keep human proportions and a human face under the helmet so its wearer passes for an ordinary soldier. It has Bionic P.S. 30, P.P. 24 and Speed 144 on nuclear power, with micro-boosters in the back and legs for long leaps; the optional 240 M.D.C. heavy armor halves its speed and costs -50% to Prowl, so it is seldom worn. This row is the body alone; the pilot is the class geofront-assault-geo-borg, which also lists the standard bionic features and the hand weapons it usually carries.', 'Rifts World Book 25: China 2 p.130-131'),
('ab-955-lion-geo-borg', 'Lion Geo-Borg (AB-955)', 'rifts', 'borg', NULL, NULL, 'Running: 140 mph (224 km). Leaping: up to 20 feet (6.1 m) high and 30 feet (9.1 m) across; increase by 50% with a running start.', 'Cannot fly.', 'Can swim at 40 mph (64 km) and survive depths of up to 800 feet (244 m).', 'Height: 4 feet (1.2 m). Width: 3 feet (0.9 m) at the hips.', '2 tons', 280, 1, NULL, 8000000, 'Mass production should get the cost down to around 8-10 million credits.', 'A human brain in the body of a giant mechanical lion, the Geofront''s newest full conversion design, made for deep reconnaissance in forest and jungle where it may pass for a Nature Spirit. It has Bionic P.S. 44, P.P. 24 and Speed 144 on nuclear power and a hide that feels like living fur, but it cannot hold weapons in its paws and is -60% on skills that need hands; about 200 prototypes are fielded and a thousand more are being built. This row is the body alone; the pilot is the class geofront-lion-geo-borg, which also lists the standard bionic features.', 'Rifts World Book 25: China 2 p.131-132');

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicle_locations (vehicle_slug, location, mdc, mdc_note, ordinal) VALUES
  ('iron-juggernaut-blazing', 'Main Body', 910, 'Regenerates 3D6 M.D. per melee round. Impervious to possession, disease, gases, toxins, cold, heat, fire, plasma, lava, magic fires and nuclear fire. Magic weapons whose magic is cold or ice inflict double damage. No other location is printed.', 1),
  ('iron-juggernaut-earthwake', 'Main Body', 1187, 'Regenerates 1D4x10 M.D. per melee round. Impervious to possession, disease, gases, toxins and normal cold and heat. Electricity, lightning, storms (including Ley Line Storms, tornadoes and hurricanes) and explosions do half damage. Most M.D. weapons and spells do normal damage; Rune weapons inflict double damage. No other location is printed.', 1),
  ('iron-juggernaut-fury', 'Main Body', 1340, 'Regenerates 6D6 M.D.C. per melee round. Cold-based magic including ice spells and weapons, wands and weapons made from a Millennium Tree, and Rune weapons all inflict double damage. No other location is printed.', 1),
  ('iron-juggernaut-iron-dragonfly', 'Main Body', 1210, 'Regenerates 4D6 M.D.C. per melee round. Magic weapons whose magic is fire or earth based inflict double damage. No other location is printed.', 1),
  ('iron-juggernaut-sea-viper', 'Main Body', 690, 'Regenerates 3D6 M.D.C. per melee round. Impervious to possession, disease, gases, toxins, pollution and ordinary cold. Electricity, sonic attacks, explosives and magic-based cold and water attacks do half damage; magic weapons and other M.D. attacks do full damage; M.D. fire, plasma, magic fires and nuclear fire do double damage. No other location is printed.', 1),
  ('iron-juggernaut-thundering', 'Main Body', 1130, 'Regenerates 5D6 M.D.C. per melee round. Impervious to possession, disease, gases, toxins, cold, heat, lightning and hurricanes; lasers do half damage. Magic weapons that are the creation of Bio-Wizardry or Rune Magic inflict double damage. No other location is printed.', 1),
  ('iron-juggernaut-warhawk', 'Main Body', 770, 'Regenerates 3D6 M.D.C. per melee round. Impervious to possession, disease, gases, toxins, cold, heat and ordinary fire. M.D. fire, plasma, magic fires, nuclear fire, electricity and sonic attacks do half damage. Magic weapons whose magic is cold, ice or water based inflict double damage, as does the fire cast by some Russian demons and gods. No other location is printed.', 1),
  ('iron-juggernaut-wing-blade', 'Main Body', 1480, 'Regenerates 3D6 M.D. per melee round. Impervious to possession, disease, gases, toxins, cold, heat, fire, plasma, lava, magic fires and nuclear fire. Magic weapons whose magic is cold or ice inflict double damage.', 1),
  ('iron-juggernaut-wing-blade', 'Wings', 200, 'each; the number of wings is not printed', 2),
